or and wealthy nations before her  life as a host producer author and  activist took off however lakshmi was  merely merely a supermodel looking to  break into the world of acting for one  of her very first television roles  lakshmi guest starred in the 2002  enterprise episode precious cargo as  princess kaitama who was kidnapped and  placed in suspended animation on the eve  of her ascension to the throne of krios  prime kaitama is rescued from captivity  by enterprise's chief engineer charles  trip tucker and the two struggle to  survive in a cramped escape pod and on a  hostile planet although lakshmi may not  be known for her acting abilities  nowadays she does an admirable job for a  novice performer she has good chemistry  with commander tucker and the two  develop a whirlwind romance that while a  little cliche and underdeveloped is  still quite entertaining to watch  despite the series being set in the  distant future the writers of star trek  occasionally found opportunities for  their characters to encounter real-life  historical figures either via time  travel or holodeck simulations actors  have portrayed such figures as author  mark twain aviator amelia earhart and  president abraham lincoln on various  episodes but only one person in the  entire history of the star trek  franchise to date has ever filmed a  cameo as themselves theoretical  physicist stephen hawking sometimes  called the world's smartest man a title  he himself rejected hawking dedicated  his life to teaching the world about the  study of space and time it's no surprise  then that hawking was a lifelong fan of  star trek a franchise that has always  prided itself on the celebration of  science in 1991 while visiting the  paramount lot hawking accepted an  invitation to tour the set of star trek  the next generation he was given the  opportunity to sit in the captain's  chair which he remarked was even comfier  than his own during his visit hawking  mentioned to executive producer rick 