on was white's guest  appearance in the season 4 star trek  enterprise episode borderland in which  he plays a massive muscular orion slaver  who attempts to sell some captured crew  members at auction white's character  repeatedly lifts commander to paul for  display during the ghastly event and it  doesn't look like any wires were used to  help him do it fans of white's work in  the squared circle know that 100 odd  pounds is barely a warm up for the big  show who claims to have bench pressed  500 pounds at the height of his athletic  prowess exaggerating physical statistics  is typical in the world of professional  wrestling but we're certainly not going  to argue with the seven-time world  champion seth macfarlane best known as  the creator and star of the animated  comedy family guy has made his lifelong  devotion to star trek no secret  introduced to the series in childhood by  his father mcfarland would go on to  create the orville a series that blends  star trek the next generation with  elements of a workplace sitcom long  before the orville first aired however  mcfarland had the opportunity to appear  in two episodes of his favorite  franchise in 2004 and 2005 mcfarland  appeared on enterprise as a starfleet  engineer called rivers ensign rivers  serves on commander tucker's engineering  team in season 3 episode the forgotten  and then evidently transfers along with  tucker to the starship columbia in the  episode affliction one year later the  enterprise appearances took place during  a career lull for mcfarlane family guy  had been canceled after three seasons in  2002 and while it was building a cult  following and reruns it wouldn't return  to the air until 2005. at the time  mcfarland was far from a recognizable  on-screen face to anyone but die-hard  fans of his work in animation but his  fortunes have no doubt reversed in the  years since  amazon founder jeff bezos is one of the  richest people in the world frequently  swapping the number one spot w