her ishka as a hostage  unlike some of the other celebrities who  have appeared on star trek pop wasn't a  fan who approached the producers for the  chance to appear instead the reverse was  true producer ira stephen bear had been  trying to cast pop a personal hero of  his on one of his shows years before he  joined star trek during the third season  of deep space nine bear and his team  wrote a part for him in the two-part  episode past tense but pop was on tour  and unavailable for shooting the role  ended up going to clint howard instead  when the magnificent ferengi went into  production pop was recovering from a  shoulder injury that forced him to take  a break from touring the rockstar  finally agreed to take the gig although  it might have just been to finally get  the producer's office case i thought the  breen were annoying  christian slater was a star on the rise  when he made a one scene cameo as a  communications officer aboard the uss  excelsior in star trek vi the  undiscovered country he'd made a splash  in 1988 as the sinister jd in the dark  high school comedy heathers and more  recently had appeared in robin hood  prince of thieves as will scarlett  however his burgeoning acting career had  little to do with his appearance on star  trek by his own admission it was pure  nepotism that got him the part his  mother mary joe slater was the casting  director for the film in the  undiscovered country christian slater  gets a short one-on-one scene opposite  george takei as a junior officer who  awakens captain sulu to deliver orders  from starfleet slater enjoyed an  additional treat on set however he got  to wear the actual outfit that william  shatner had worn in star trek ii the  wrath of khan slater was so thrilled in  fact that he was unwilling to part with  it and simply walked off set still in  costume when no one was looking  as of 2017 he's still got it stashed  away given slater's more recent  appearances in tv dramas like mr robot  and dr dea