 was  on set for only a few hours had his two  lines and was out before lunch  of course scott's affection for star  trek isn't limited to his brief  appearance in first contact his parks  and rec character ben wyatt has a  certain appreciation for the sci-fi  franchise himself are you busy  and writing star trek fan fiction does  not count  i  finished it last week what's going on  in the early 1990s there was no bigger  show on television than cheers the nbc  sitcom that drew an unreal 80.4 million  viewers for its series finale among the  show's most popular characters was dr  frasier crane played by kelsey grammer  who would go on to star in his own  long-running spin-off frasier star trek  the next generation was certainly a pop  culture phenomena but cheers was on a  whole other level that's why it must  have been a real treat for fans when  grammar made a somewhat comical cameo at  the end of the season 5 episode cause  and effect he appears as captain morgan  bateson the commanding officer of a  starship that's been caught in a time  loop for nearly a century grammar is the  third cheers actor to appear in a star  trek production the first being kirstie  alley who made her acting debut as savic  in star trek ii the wrath of khan the  producers wanted ali to appear in the  episode with grammar as well reprising  her role as savic but ally's busy  schedule didn't allow for it not only  would this have been a cute in-joke for  fans of tears but it also might have  finally answered the question of what  actually happened to her character in  the years that followed several members  of the star trek ensemble would go on to  make appearances on frasier including  next generation stars patrick stewart  and brent spiner check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite shows  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

